{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004809-indirect-magickal-damage","id":1004809,"title":"Indirect Magickal Damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T22:22:22-08:00","id":1004809,"title":"Indirect Magickal Damage","content":"RAW has rules for obvious applications of magickal force (fireballs, lightning, telekinetic missiles, Prime augmented strikes, direct Life or Entropy attacks, etc), that are either performed on the target, done over an area, or aimed. When it comes to Damage, we consult the damage and duration chart, soak rolls as needed. So far so good.<br /> <br /> But what about all the specific ways that Mages can harm their opponent? Effects wherein the harm a character experiences is a side benefit of making the magick happen? Using Matter to turn the air into acid or a flammable gas (that is then ignited through mundane means). Prime used to conjure heavy objects over a person's head, or liters of water inside their lungs. Correspondence teleporting a target 100 meters in the air, so that they potentially fall to their deaths. Spirit forcing a target over the Gauntlet and into a Penumbra area with ephemeral environmental hazards. Forces altering gravity so a person flies sideways onto sharp objects or surfaces. Anything having to do with Radiation. A whole lot of edge cases that are entirely viable options (albeit usually Vulgar), yet the books don't really have rules for. Or the rules that exist need to be bent and twisted so they apply.<br /> <br /> Short of just rolling damage anyway (which smacks of RBD, and we've had this discussion before), how do you all handle this kind of thing? Have you any stories that feature interesting (and possibly amusing) applications of Sphere powers? And are there any other fringe cases I haven't already covered, but which would apply?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T00:58:08-08:00","id":1004834,"title":"","content":"There's Environmental Hazards section in M20 which includes damage from starving, dehydration, poisons/ toxins/ radiation, damage from falls and vehicle collisions, charts for objects of all kinds (what kind of damage person gets if you smash them into something with a Forces push, or what if you make it fall on them), there are even rules about how damage increases according to object's speed and distance travelled.<br /> <br /> It goes after combat section, which is 400+ page. You could also just open book pages index at page 5 and search &quot;Environmental Hazards&quot; (might have slightly different name, forgot). You can find all of the required information there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:41:18-08:00","id":1004849,"title":"","content":"Alternatively you could just think &quot;hmm, a 50 foot drop... That's probably three dice of lethal&quot; and just leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Just think about what's just happened and make a judgement call. This ain't DnD, we don't need charts for every eventuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-18-2016, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:58:04-08:00","id":1004856,"title":"","content":"If you teleport a BHO (Big Heavy Object) over some guards, then give them a dramatic death.<br /> The Arch-villain would most certainly offer more resistance.<br /> In such cases it is dramatically fitting to let him dodge by a micrometer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:46:20-08:00","id":1004912,"title":"","content":"Falling damage is listed and water in the lungs I would just run as drowning the other stuff like the BHO I judge on the fly and probably agree with it being an auto kill for non special targets and really bad for players and named NPCs. Air to acid and other such attcks I just convet success to damage like normal. It may not be the most realistic but its quick and simple. I'd rather do that then waste time figuring something else out. Besides its not like this kind of stuff is super common. At least not in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:13:41-08:00","id":1004920,"title":"","content":"Standard WoD falling damage is a joke. An insane, utter joke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A human falling 80 feet will be incapacitated. For a single day. If they don't soak some of the bashing damage. Roflmayo.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Which is why I once wrote a houserule:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For reference, a person falling from 30 feet (10 meters) equals getting hit by a MAC truck at ~30 mph (50 km/h). Except the MAC truck is planet sized.<br /> In the default WoD rules this supposedly results in having to soak 3 whole bashing damage. Golfclap.<br /> Scarily enough, after 9 feet (3 meters) you're already going 17 mph (28km/h).<br /> There is a reason we instinctively are scared of jumping down even moderate heights.<br /> <br /> So, new rules, with a concrete floor as default:<br /> <br /> 1) At 3 feet (1 meter), nothing bad happens. Let's not overdo it.<br /> 2) For every 3 feet (1 meter) after that, falling damage increases by +1 lethal damage<br /> 3) The damage gets reduced through a successful Dexterity+Athletics roll, pre-soak.<br /> de<br /> *) Uncontrolled/sudden falling doubles the amount of damage<br /> *) A botch in the Dexterity+Athletics roll doubles the amount of damage. Yes, those two things stack.<br /> *) Softer ground, soft obstacles slowing the fall etc. can turn the damage to bashing and/or reduce it further. Uneven ground, rocks, falling into a pile of scissors, etc. make things worse. Ask your ST for details. </div> </div> </div>EDIT2:<br /> <br /> This rule could also be inverted and modified to calculate the damage from falling (accordingly heavy or sharp) objects. Because physics don't care much if you fall head first onto a bowling-ball, or a bowling-ball falls onto your head (aside of air-friction and inertia differences, but let's not make things too complex..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-18-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:53:54-08:00","id":1005027,"title":"","content":"Okay, to clear up a misunderstanding, <i>yes I know and have already read the Environmental Hazards section of M20</i>. My assertion is that this section doesn't cover all edge cases. It doesn't say, for instance, how to calculate damage inflicted by objects falling on a person. (And no, just winging seems insufficient, especially if NPCs start trying it on the player characters). Or the effects of acid or radiation. (The closest it gets to addressing radiation is in the Explosion section, where a nuke's damage is given as &quot;Seriously?&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T11:11:49-08:00","id":1005033,"title":"","content":"Problem is that if you want a system for every kind of edge case, you're going to be spending more time looking up systems than actually playing out the scenario.<br /> <br /> For example, if you want a system for objects falling on people, what are the things you're going to want to consider? Relative mass? Velocity? Hardness of the material? How sharp it is? Whether it lands on their head? How soft the ground is (on a scale of Water to diamond)...<br /> <br /> That's a lot of variables to keep in mind for something which only takes a few seconds of in game time. Combat already takes up a huge amount of time as it is. Just think about it in terms of Health levels lost. So if you expect this sort of damage to injure them, its 3 dice, and if you expected it to cripple them, then 6 dice. Keep it simple and maintain the flow of the game.<br /> <br /> As for a Nuke going off, unless they're doing some sort of magic to protect themselves, have all people in the immediate blast radius as &quot;dead, very very dead&quot;. Anyone in the secondary radius will instead have radiation poisoning, which you can easily adapt the disease rules to fit (having them get gradually increasing bouts of damage each day for as long as they are poisoned, you can start with bashing or move straight to lethal depending on how severe the initial dose was).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:08:47-08:00","id":1005159,"title":"","content":"I always forget falling damage is bashing until what 100 feet or so. I've always ran it as lethal after 10' . And regular armor wont help. I see why they do it how the do since really its more how you land than how far you fall so they keep bashing so its soakable to represent it.<br /> <br /> Another method would be to run it how it is but if you dont saok all the damage you take all the damage. Lets face it. Falls usually hurt alot or not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:00:33-08:00","id":1005221,"title":"","content":"Tell that to my knees, which seem quite good at finding the middle ground.<br /> <br /> Falling is such a crapshoot it's hard to have a realistic system that covers all possibilities. I mean, people trip and crack their skulls all the time, but people have also survived skydiving accidents where their parachutes didn't open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T22:02:55-08:00","id":1005239,"title":"","content":"Really, the falling character should roll Dexterity + Athletics at the moment of impact, to simulate their efforts to roll with the landing and disperse force less harmfully. Each success reduces the difficulty of the resulting soak roll by -1, or alternatively just negates health levels of damage before soak. It depends on how charitable the storyteller wants to be. Obviously a person without Athletics shouldn't be able to perform this maneuver. Still, once it gets to the lethal damage range, the character relies on negating the force of the fall (unless they can soak lethal because of armor/magic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}